				<title>(no title)</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13481719/6-1-2#post-4722257</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Fri, 17 Jul 2020 18:50:15 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>not_a_seagull</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3009022</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Tenative upvote. There were a lot of places where the grammar could use a bit of touching up. This part in particular stuck out to me, as a run-on sentence:</p> <blockquote> <p>They pinned their Foundation ID to their hoodie—it was outdated, with an old picture and the title still reading AGENT - MU-4 (“DEBUGGERS”), they’d have to get that fixed eventually—and stood, unsteadily, with Maisy nervously circling their legs</p> </blockquote> <p>That being said, the pacing was alright all the way through, and I like the core idea. Even if <a href="http://www.scpwiki.com/scp-3199">SCP-3199</a> is overused nowadays.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
